//! mycelium/lapse_knot.rye -- the deadline verdict reads across a Knot (rung r3).
//!
//! Season D (Kresfa & Mycelium) - Mycelium consensus - the deadline verdict - rung r3.
//! Design read: active-designing/date/20260813/20260813-085046_mycelium-lapse-pending-timeout-exploration.md
//!
//! Rung 1 resolved a whole Cord Dag into a deadline-clock Ledger -- which pledges reserved
//! coins, which were honored, released, or LAPSED when the order's clock passed their
//! deadline. Yet a ledger a family runs for years does not carry its whole past unbroken:
//! the Knot (`cord_knot.rye`) ties off a committed prefix into a sealed `fold.FoldState` so a
//! bounded Dag runs forever, and new facts continue onto that seal. This rung makes the
//! Lapse's corpus a Knot plus its live suffix -- the checkpointed accounts and open pledges
//! read through the same verdict, their deadlines still keeping time across the cut.
//!
//! The crux is a deadline that reaches ACROSS the cut. A pledge opens under a deadline inside
//! the SEALED prefix (coins reserved, the promise still young); the past is tied off and
//! pruned; then the order's clock passes the deadline in the LIVE suffix, and the pledge
//! LAPSES there -- the reserved coins home to the pledger, on time, though the deadline was
//! set before the checkpoint and reached after it. Every honest node names the same outcome
//! whether it reads the whole Cord or a Knot plus a live suffix.
//!
//! The honest seam this crux surfaces, new to the Lapse: the Pledge's timing was irrelevant
//! to its verdict, so `pledge_knot` folds its suffix at LOCAL positions (the pruned prefix's
//! global order is simply gone). The Lapse cannot -- its deadline is an ABSOLUTE order
//! position, so the clock must not restart at the cut. So a `LapseKnot` carries one thing
//! more than the two-phase Knot did: the epoch BASE, the count of order positions the sealed
//! prefix consumed. The suffix continues the clock at `base + i`, so a deadline set before the
//! cut still fires at exactly the order position it named -- the checkpoint prunes the past
//! without resetting the hour. As in `pledge_knot`, the Knot seals only fold's GLOBAL supply
//! law (issued - taxed - reserved stars), whose `issued` equals the prefix's `total_issued`;
//! the account-and-pledge map (with each pledge's deadline) travels beside it.
//!
//! Additive by construction: it imports `lapse` (r1's `Ledger` / `fold_lapse` /
//! `balances_sum`), `cord_knot`, `cord`, and `fold`, and calls only their public API. Rung
//! one stays its own green binary; the Knot stays its own green binary. No storage, no
//! transport, no network, no custody -- a node reads across its own sealed checkpoint. Demo
//! keeper seeds only -- no real key, no funds.
//!
//!   env RYE_ZIG=vendor/zig-toolchain/zig rye/bin/rye run mycelium/lapse_knot.rye

const std = @import("std");
const assert = std.debug.assert;
const print = std.debug.print;
const cord = @import("cord.rye");
const cord_knot = @import("cord_knot.rye");
const fold = @import("fold.rye");
const lapse = @import("lapse.rye");
const kumara = @import("kumara.rye");
const tally_copy = @import("tally_copy.rye");

/// A checkpointed deadline verdict: the Knot sealing the prefix's global supply law under a
/// digest, beside the prefix's account-and-pledge map (with each pledge's deadline), and the
/// epoch BASE -- the count of order positions the prefix consumed, so the live suffix
/// continues the clock unbroken at `base + i`.
pub const LapseKnot = struct {
    knot: cord_knot.Knot = .{},
    verdict: lapse.Ledger = .{},
    base: u64 = 0,
};

/// The count of order positions a committed prefix consumes -- the epoch base the suffix
/// continues the clock from. Computed with the Cord's own deterministic commit, so the base
/// is the same number `lapse.resolve` walked.
fn committed_len(dag: *const cord.Dag) u64 {
    // invariant: the prefix Dag fits the static bound before it is committed.
    assert(dag.len <= cord.cord_max_blocks);
    var order: [cord.cord_max_blocks]u32 = undefined;
    const committed = cord.commit(dag, order[0..]);
    // invariant: a committed count never exceeds the blocks it ordered.
    assert(committed <= dag.len);
    return committed;
}

/// Seal a committed prefix Dag into a LapseKnot -- resolve it to its deadline verdict, tie off
/// its global supply with a Knot, and record the epoch base. The prefix's accounts and open
/// pledges (deadlines intact) travel in `verdict`; the sealed `FoldState` in `knot` is the
/// integrity-checked starting supply; `base` is where the suffix resumes the clock. A prefix
/// that itself overdrew globally refuses at `seal_dag`.
pub fn seal_lapse(dag: *const cord.Dag) (lapse.FoldError || error{ LogFull, StarTaken })!LapseKnot {
    // invariant: the prefix Dag fits the static bound before it is committed.
    assert(dag.len <= cord.cord_max_blocks);
    const v = try lapse.resolve(dag);
    const k = try cord_knot.seal_dag(dag);
    const base = committed_len(dag);
    // invariant: the sealed Knot verifies the instant it is made.
    assert(cord_knot.verify(&k));
    // invariant: the sealed global issue equals the per-account issue -- the number
    // conservation is measured against travels integrity-checked.
    assert(k.state.issued == v.total_issued);
    return .{ .knot = k, .verdict = v, .base = base };
}

/// Continue the deadline verdict onto a checkpoint -- verify the Knot, seed a Ledger with the
/// prefix's accounts and open pledges, then walk the live suffix through `lapse.fold_lapse` at
/// positions `base + i`, so the clock resumes exactly where the prefix left it. A suffix fact
/// whose position reaches an open pledge's deadline LAPSES it across the cut; a suffix post
/// before the deadline honors a pledge opened before the cut; a suffix void releases it. A
/// corrupt Knot refuses before a single fact is folded; an unknown or wrong-signed or
/// amount-mismatched resolution, a bad-deadline pledge, a broken signature, a star reserve,
/// and a malformed body each still refuse whole. Conservation holds past the cut.
pub fn continue_lapse(lk: *const LapseKnot, suffix: *const fold.Log) (error{KnotCorrupt} || lapse.FoldError)!lapse.Ledger {
    // invariant: the suffix stays within the fold's own log bound.
    assert(suffix.len <= fold.myc_log_max_facts);
    // invariant: the sealed prefix state is a lawful fold state before it is trusted.
    assert(lk.knot.state.taxed <= lk.knot.state.issued);
    // invariant: the whole continued epoch fits the fold's position ceiling.
    assert(lk.base + suffix.len <= fold.myc_log_max_facts);
    // The Knot is untrusted input -- a tampered one violates its own digest by design, so its
    // integrity is a runtime GATE (verify), never an assert. A corrupt Knot refuses whole
    // before a single suffix fact is folded.
    if (!cord_knot.verify(&lk.knot)) return error.KnotCorrupt;

    var l = lk.verdict; // the prefix account-and-pledge map, deadlines intact, across the cut
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < suffix.len) : (i += 1) {
        // The clock does not restart at the cut: the suffix fact at local index `i` folds at
        // absolute order position `base + i`, so a deadline named before the checkpoint still
        // fires at exactly the position it chose. This is the whole reason a LapseKnot carries
        // the base the two-phase Knot did not.
        const pos: u32 = @intCast(lk.base + i);
        try lapse.fold_lapse(&l, &suffix.facts[i], pos);
    }
    // invariant: conservation -- balance + reserved still sums to what genesis issued.
    assert(l.balances_sum() + l.reserved_sum() == l.total_issued);
    return l;
}

/// The deadline verdict never drifts between a full Cord and a Knot-continued resolution: the
/// pledge and settlement counts (posted - voided - lapsed), the issued total, each account's
/// balance and reserve, and every pledge's settlement, amount, and deadline agree. Position is
/// deliberately not compared -- it is local to each epoch's own numbering.
pub fn lapses_match(whole: *const lapse.Ledger, across: *const lapse.Ledger) bool {
    // invariant: both verdicts stay within the named ceilings.
    assert(whole.pledge_count <= lapse.lapse_max_pledges);
    assert(across.pledge_count <= lapse.lapse_max_pledges);
    if (whole.pledges_seen() != across.pledges_seen()) return false;
    if (whole.posted_seen() != across.posted_seen()) return false;
    if (whole.voided_seen() != across.voided_seen()) return false;
    if (whole.lapsed_seen() != across.lapsed_seen()) return false;
    if (whole.total_issued != across.total_issued) return false;
    if (whole.account_count != across.account_count) return false;
    // Every account holds the same spendable and reserved coins on both nodes.
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < whole.account_count) : (i += 1) {
        const wk = whole.accounts[i].pk[0..];
        if (whole.accounts[i].balance != across.balance_of(wk)) return false;
        if (whole.accounts[i].reserved != across.reserved_of(wk)) return false;
    }
    // Each pledge's settlement, amount, and deadline is the verdict's fingerprint.
    i = 0;
    while (i < whole.pledge_count) : (i += 1) {
        const wp = whole.pledge_at(i) orelse return false;
        const ap = across.pledge_at(i) orelse return false;
        if (wp.state != ap.state) return false;
        if (wp.amount != ap.amount) return false;
        if (wp.deadline != ap.deadline) return false;
        if (!std.mem.eql(u8, wp.id[0..], ap.id[0..])) return false;
    }
    return true;
}

// ---- selftest: the deadline verdict reads the same across a sealed checkpoint ----

fn seeded(byte: u8) kumara.KeyPair {
    const seed: [kumara.seed_length]u8 = .{byte} ** kumara.seed_length;
    return kumara.keypair_from_seed(&seed);
}

fn write_deadline(deadline: u64, out: []u8) void {
    // invariant: the buffer holds a full little-endian order position.
    assert(out.len == lapse.deadline_len);
    var v = deadline;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < lapse.deadline_len) : (i += 1) {
        out[i] = @truncate(v);
        v >>= 8;
    }
}

fn pledge_body(id: []const u8, deadline: u64, to: []const u8, out: []u8) u32 {
    // invariant: the buffer holds tag - id - deadline - recipient exactly.
    assert(out.len >= 1 + lapse.id_len + lapse.deadline_len + lapse.pk_len);
    assert(id.len == lapse.id_len);
    out[0] = lapse.tag_pledge;
    tally_copy.copy_disjoint(u8, out[1 .. 1 + lapse.id_len], id);
    write_deadline(deadline, out[1 + lapse.id_len .. 1 + lapse.id_len + lapse.deadline_len]);
    tally_copy.copy_disjoint(u8, out[1 + lapse.id_len + lapse.deadline_len ..][0..lapse.pk_len], to);
    return 1 + lapse.id_len + lapse.deadline_len + lapse.pk_len;
}

fn resolve_body(tag: u8, id: []const u8, out: []u8) u32 {
    // invariant: the buffer holds tag - id exactly.
    assert(out.len >= 1 + lapse.id_len);
    assert(id.len == lapse.id_len);
    out[0] = tag;
    tally_copy.copy_disjoint(u8, out[1 .. 1 + lapse.id_len], id);
    return 1 + lapse.id_len;
}

/// Seat the scene: genesis credits Alice 100 (round 0); Alice pledges 100 to Bob under the
/// given deadline (round 1); Alice posts it (round 2). The prefix is genesis + pledge (base 2),
/// the suffix the post -- so a deadline of 2 is reached in the suffix (lapse across the cut),
/// and a far deadline is honored in the suffix (kept across the cut).
fn seat(id: []const u8, deadline: u64) !struct { g: cord.Block, pledge: cord.Block, post: cord.Block, void_block: cord.Block, post_fact: fold.Fact, void_fact: fold.Fact } {
    const kf = seeded(0xF0);
    const ka = seeded(0xA1);
    const kb = seeded(0xB2);
    const alice_pk = ka.public_key.toBytes();
    const bob_pk = kb.public_key.toBytes();

    const f_gen = fold.mint_fact(kf, fold.kind_issue, 100, "", alice_pk[0..]) orelse return error.MintGen;
    var pb: [1 + lapse.id_len + lapse.deadline_len + lapse.pk_len]u8 = undefined;
    const pn = pledge_body(id, deadline, bob_pk[0..], &pb);
    const f_pledge = fold.mint_fact(ka, fold.kind_tax, 100, "", pb[0..pn]) orelse return error.MintPledge;
    var hb: [1 + lapse.id_len]u8 = undefined;
    const hn = resolve_body(lapse.tag_post, id, &hb);
    const f_post = fold.mint_fact(ka, fold.kind_tax, 100, "", hb[0..hn]) orelse return error.MintPost;
    var vb: [1 + lapse.id_len]u8 = undefined;
    const vn = resolve_body(lapse.tag_void, id, &vb);
    const f_void = fold.mint_fact(ka, fold.kind_tax, 100, "", vb[0..vn]) orelse return error.MintVoid;

    const g = cord.mint_block(kf, 0, &[_][cord.hash_len]u8{}, f_gen) orelse return error.BlockG;
    var hg: [cord.hash_len]u8 = undefined;
    cord.address(&g, &hg);
    const roots = [_][cord.hash_len]u8{hg};
    const b_pledge = cord.mint_block(ka, 1, roots[0..], f_pledge) orelse return error.BlockPledge;
    var hpl: [cord.hash_len]u8 = undefined;
    cord.address(&b_pledge, &hpl);
    const roots2 = [_][cord.hash_len]u8{hpl};
    const b_post = cord.mint_block(ka, 2, roots2[0..], f_post) orelse return error.BlockPost;
    const b_void = cord.mint_block(ka, 2, roots2[0..], f_void) orelse return error.BlockVoid;
    return .{ .g = g, .pledge = b_pledge, .post = b_post, .void_block = b_void, .post_fact = f_post, .void_fact = f_void };
}

pub fn main() !void {
    const id = [_]u8{0x01} ** lapse.id_len;
    const id2 = [_]u8{0x02} ** lapse.id_len;
    const ka = seeded(0xA1);
    const kb = seeded(0xB2);
    const alice_pk = ka.public_key.toBytes();
    const bob_pk = kb.public_key.toBytes();

    // --- The crux: a deadline set before the cut, reached after it ---------------
    // Deadline 2. Prefix = genesis + pledge (base 2). The pledge stands OPEN at the seal (no
    // order position past 1 was walked). The suffix post rides absolute position base+0 = 2,
    // so the clock reaches the deadline there and LAPSES the pledge across the cut -- the coins
    // home to Alice, the late post a no-op.
    {
        const s = try seat(id[0..], 2);

        // The truth to match: the WHOLE history resolved as one Cord -- the post at position 2
        // finds the deadline (2) already reached, so the pledge lapses.
        var whole = cord.Dag.empty();
        try cord.add(&whole, s.g);
        try cord.add(&whole, s.pledge);
        try cord.add(&whole, s.post);
        const whole_verdict = try lapse.resolve(&whole);
        if (whole_verdict.lapsed_seen() != 1) return error.WholeLapsed;
        if (whole_verdict.balance_of(alice_pk[0..]) != 100) return error.WholeAlice;
        if (whole_verdict.balance_of(bob_pk[0..]) != 0) return error.WholeBob;

        // The Knot path: seal the prefix (genesis + pledge), then continue the post.
        var prefix = cord.Dag.empty();
        try cord.add(&prefix, s.g);
        try cord.add(&prefix, s.pledge);
        const lk = try seal_lapse(&prefix);
        if (lk.base != 2) return error.PrefixBase;
        // At the seal the pledge is OPEN -- reserved, the deadline not yet reached.
        if (lk.verdict.open_seen() != 1) return error.PrefixOpen;
        if (lk.verdict.lapsed_seen() != 0) return error.PrefixLapsed;
        if (lk.verdict.reserved_of(alice_pk[0..]) != 100) return error.PrefixReserve;
        if (lk.knot.state.issued != 100) return error.PrefixIssued;

        var suffix = fold.Log.empty();
        suffix.facts[0] = s.post_fact;
        suffix.len = 1;
        const across = try continue_lapse(&lk, &suffix);

        // The crux: the deadline named before the cut fires in the suffix -- the pledge lapses
        // across the checkpoint, the coins home to Alice, the post a lawful no-op.
        if (across.lapsed_seen() != 1) return error.AcrossLapsed;
        if (across.posted_seen() != 0) return error.AcrossPosted;
        if (across.balance_of(alice_pk[0..]) != 100) return error.AcrossAlice;
        if (across.reserved_of(alice_pk[0..]) != 0) return error.AcrossReserve;
        if (across.balance_of(bob_pk[0..]) != 0) return error.AcrossBob;
        if (across.balances_sum() + across.reserved_sum() != 100) return error.AcrossNotConserved;

        // The verdict never drifts between the full Cord and the Knot-continued one.
        if (!lapses_match(&whole_verdict, &across)) return error.KnotChangedVerdict;

        // Integrity across the cut: a Knot corrupted after sealing refuses whole.
        var lk_bad = lk;
        lk_bad.knot.state.issued += 1;
        if (continue_lapse(&lk_bad, &suffix)) |_| return error.CorruptTrusted else |err| {
            if (err != error.KnotCorrupt) return error.WrongCorrupt;
        }

        // A tampered suffix fact (its own signature broken) refuses IdentityRefused.
        var f_tamper = s.post_fact;
        f_tamper.sig[0] ^= 0xff;
        var suffix_tamper = fold.Log.empty();
        suffix_tamper.facts[0] = f_tamper;
        suffix_tamper.len = 1;
        if (continue_lapse(&lk, &suffix_tamper)) |_| return error.TamperTrusted else |err| {
            if (err != error.IdentityRefused) return error.WrongTamper;
        }

        // A suffix resolution of a pledge the checkpoint never opened refuses UnknownPledge.
        var hb2: [1 + lapse.id_len]u8 = undefined;
        const hn2 = resolve_body(lapse.tag_post, id2[0..], &hb2);
        const f_ghost = fold.mint_fact(ka, fold.kind_tax, 100, "", hb2[0..hn2]) orelse return error.MintGhost;
        var suffix_ghost = fold.Log.empty();
        suffix_ghost.facts[0] = f_ghost;
        suffix_ghost.len = 1;
        if (continue_lapse(&lk, &suffix_ghost)) |_| return error.GhostCrossed else |err| {
            if (err != error.UnknownPledge) return error.WrongGhost;
        }
    }

    // --- The companion: a deadline far enough that the suffix HONORS across the cut ---
    // Deadline 5. Prefix = genesis + pledge (base 2). The suffix post rides position 2 < 5, so
    // the pledge is still alive and the post honors it -- a promise made before the cut, kept
    // after it, exactly as the two-phase Knot showed, now under a deadline that had time.
    {
        const s = try seat(id[0..], 5);
        var prefix = cord.Dag.empty();
        try cord.add(&prefix, s.g);
        try cord.add(&prefix, s.pledge);
        const lk = try seal_lapse(&prefix);

        var suffix = fold.Log.empty();
        suffix.facts[0] = s.post_fact;
        suffix.len = 1;
        const honored = try continue_lapse(&lk, &suffix);
        if (honored.posted_seen() != 1) return error.HonoredPosted;
        if (honored.lapsed_seen() != 0) return error.HonoredLapsed;
        if (honored.balance_of(bob_pk[0..]) != 100) return error.HonoredBob;
        if (honored.reserved_of(alice_pk[0..]) != 0) return error.HonoredReserve;
        if (honored.balances_sum() + honored.reserved_sum() != 100) return error.HonoredNotConserved;

        // A void in the suffix releases the still-alive pledge instead -- reserved home to
        // Alice, an atomic reversal spanning the checkpoint.
        var suffix_void = fold.Log.empty();
        suffix_void.facts[0] = s.void_fact;
        suffix_void.len = 1;
        const released = try continue_lapse(&lk, &suffix_void);
        if (released.voided_seen() != 1) return error.ReleasedVoided;
        if (released.balance_of(alice_pk[0..]) != 100) return error.ReleasedAlice;
        if (released.balances_sum() + released.reserved_sum() != 100) return error.ReleasedNotConserved;
    }

    print("lapse-knot: the prefix seals a Knot holding Alice's coin reserved in one open pledge under a deadline; the suffix reaches that deadline and the pledge LAPSES across the cut, the coins home to Alice\n", .{});
    print("lapse-knot: the deadline verdict reads the same across the cut — a full Cord and a sealed Knot name one lapsed pledge, the clock carried unbroken by the epoch base; a far deadline honors the suffix post instead, conservation of balance + reserved whole\n", .{});
    print("lapse-knot: a corrupt Knot, a tampered suffix fact, and a resolution of a pledge the checkpoint never opened each refuse whole\n", .{});
    print("GREEN: myc lapse-knot — the deadline verdict reads across a Knot, the hour kept unbroken by the epoch base · verdict never drifts\n", .{});
}
